aine? An antediluvian? A Methuselah? That's the fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was once a Cainite who claimed to be Caine. He was very... convincing. If he was the cabbie that would be a twist of plot \ud83d\ude42.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T16:48:29-07:00","id":1394874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394634-messerach?p=1394862#post1394862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was once a Cainite who claimed to be Caine. He was very... convincing. If he was the cabbie that would be a twist of plot \ud83d\ude42.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any ancient could do a good enough impression to cow any ancilla or neonate. Plus how big an apocalypse do you need? A meth can do a city easy, an ante can do a nation, when you are next to them, what's the difference","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:01:06-07:00","id":1394881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394634-messerach?p=1394862#post1394862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was once a Cainite who claimed to be Caine. He was very... convincing. If he was the cabbie that would be a twist of plot \ud83d\ude42.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of like the idea Caine just finds the whole Antediluvian &quot;rule the world&quot; thing to be nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:47:47-07:00","id":1394912,"title":"","content":"Here's a theory:<br /> <br /> It is possible Messerach was a normal human corpse, and the coffin was opened from inside. It's also possible the mummy could be posed in multiple ways without cracking and crumbling.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni could have animated the corpse. This is why it had to take a detour to the Giovanni mansion. While there the Giovanni had the mummy open the sarcophagus from the inside and climb out. Hell, maybe they had the mummy mow their lawn, who knows?<br /> <br /> Jack arranged the whole deal:<ul><li>The Giovanni knew where the box was. How? Used a Necromancy seance and asked Mess's wraith where his body was. Problem is, they couldn't go get the box themselves, since if they were caught it would be very, very bad.</li> <li>Jack arranged for the sarcophagus (with Mess. inside) to reach the Giovanni. How? He told the Nagaraja about the items at the Giovanni mansion and the museum, and suggested she send the Protagonist to go get them. The break-in at the museum distracted Beckett long enough that Jack (or, more likely, an anarch agent) could steal the sarcophogus and deliver it to the Giovanni.</li> <li>The Giovanni animated the mummy and had him open the box from the inside. The Giovanni kept the mummy, after weighing him.</li> <li>Jack is given access to the open sarcophagus, and replaces the exact weight of the mummy with explosives. He recloses and seals the lid.</li> <li>The Giovanni keep the profits from selling the coffin to the highest bidder. Pretty much anybody who would be the highest bidder and get the box and the key in one place is someone Jack wants blown up.</li> </ul><br /> Jack, realizing the opportunity has arisen, goes back to the Giovanni mansion after the protagonist &quot;deals with&quot; the Giovanni and gets the mummy. The mummy is still animated at that point, like the other zombies in the mansion, so Jack ties him to a chair for storage until he quiets down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:25:48-07:00","id":1394966,"title":"","content":"Part of me likes to go back to the idea of &quot;the night is dark and full of terrors... besides vampires.&quot; So he might be a wraith or spectre, a lich, or something else.<br /> <br /> Part of the loves the poetry of him jut being the bones of a mortal and nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:29:37-07:00","id":1394970,"title":"","content":"I agree with Grumpy RPG Reviews...<br /> <br /> And a third part of me wishes the coffin had a false bottom: we saw just a mortal corpse, and the lich (mummy, spectre, Risen, Harbinger of Skulls, etc...) was lurking underneath, all the while giggling madly (or not so madly...) to emself...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T00:54:57-07:00","id":1395031,"title":"","content":"Count me in as liking the idea of Messerach being a normal human king with no connection to the supernatural at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T00:59:39-07:00","id":1395033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394634-messerach?p=1395031#post1395031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Count me in as liking the idea of Messerach being a normal human king with no connection to the supernatural at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, I think the answer was there all along. That ignorant and confused Swedish archaeologist extensively examined the coffin and had the key.<br /> <br /> So he knew the truth but no one paused to LISTEN to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T01:19:27-07:00","id":1395035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394634-messerach?p=1394970#post1394970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Grumpy RPG Reviews...<br /> <br /> And a third part of me wishes the coffin had a false bottom: we saw just a mortal corpse, and the lich (mummy, spectre, Risen, Harbinger of Skulls, etc...) was lurking underneath, all the while giggling madly (or not so madly...) to emself...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right up until the C-4 went off anyway. Oops. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T14:12:05-07:00","id":1395146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394634-messerach?p=1394912#post1394912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a theory:<br /> <br /> It is possible Messerach was a normal human corpse, and the coffin was opened from inside. It's also possible the mummy could be posed in multiple ways without cracking and crumbling.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni could have animated the corpse. This is why it had to take a detour to the Giovanni mansion. While there the Giovanni had the mummy open the sarcophagus from the inside and climb out. Hell, maybe they had the mummy mow their lawn, who knows?<br /> <br /> Jack arranged the whole deal:<ul><li>The Giovanni knew where the box was. How? Used a Necromancy seance and asked Mess's wraith where his body was. Problem is, they couldn't go get the box themselves, since if they were caught it would be very, very bad.</li> <li>Jack arranged for the sarcophagus (with Mess. inside) to reach the Giovanni. How? He told the Nagaraja about the items at the Giovanni mansion and the museum, and suggested she send the Protagonist to go get them. The break-in at the museum distracted Beckett long enough that Jack (or, more likely, an anarch agent) could steal the sarcophogus and deliver it to the Giovanni.</li> <li>The Giovanni animated the mummy and had him open the box from the inside. The Giovanni kept the mummy, after weighing him.</li> <li>Jack is given access to the open sarcophagus, and replaces the exact weight of the mummy with explosives. He recloses and seals the lid.</li> <li>The Giovanni keep the profits from selling the coffin to the highest bidder. Pretty much anybody who would be the highest bidder and get the box and the key in one place is someone Jack wants blown up.</li> </ul>Jack, realizing the opportunity has arisen, goes back to the Giovanni mansion after the protagonist &quot;deals with&quot; the Giovanni and gets the mummy. The mummy is still animated at that point, like the other zombies in the mansion, so Jack ties him to a chair for storage until he quiets down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love your way of thinking. But in that case I would throw away the mummy and find another solution. For example the corpse could be put out of the sarcophagus and the marks suggesting it was opened from the inside was made by Jack. I don't think anyone would check it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 06-08-2020, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T14:12:48-07:00","id":1395147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394634-messerach?p=1394970#post1394970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Grumpy RPG Reviews...<br /> <br /> And a third part of me wishes the coffin had a false bottom: we saw just a mortal corpse, and the lich (mummy, spectre, Risen, Harbinger of Skulls, etc...) was lurking underneath, all the while giggling madly (or not so madly...) to emself...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T00:31:56-07:00","id":1395263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394634-messerach?p=1395033#post1395033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, I think the answer was there all along. That ignorant and confused Swedish archaeologist extensively examined the coffin and had the key.<br /> <br /> So he knew the truth but no one paused to LISTEN to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much so although he was Norweigan and not Swedish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T12:23:42-07:00","id":1457503,"title":"","content":"The simple fact the Sarcophagus has a <b>key</b> in the first place implies the object is anything but, if you stop to think about it. In a chronicle of mine the corpse is a red herring to hide it was <i>never </i>a sarcophagus in the first place, but some sort of libation/sacrificial vessel, an artifact-gift of Lamashtu to her beloved servants.<br /> <br /> Smiling Jack has been bamboozled as a pawn in someone else's game too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-23-2021, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T17:13:02-07:00","id":1457528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394634-messerach?p=1394676#post1394676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, that explains all but one thing: why the body didn't decompose after being put out of the sarcophagus, especially if we consider the fact that the ending happens a few nights after Jack's visit to Elizabeth Dane. You may be right, it's his style. Still I find it a little trivial to end the story like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You shouldn't base your knowledge in adventure movies and then judge others' research. In this case the game is quite right.<br /> <br /> Mummies aren't barely-holding dust cakes, they're highly well preserved corpses. Since the Middle Ages, by the way, Europe had some trade on ancient mummies that rarely gave them anything resembling careful handling and they hold up just fine. Archaeologists wouldn't do that <b><i><u>today</u></i></b> because they want to preserve as much data as possible, for as much time as possible, not because they crumble with a touch.<br /> <br /> By the way, the people that used real mummies to make remedies (yes. That was a thing. That was a thing until the 20th century. On the black market that is STILL a thing) had to use regular meat and bone grinders to do so.<br /> <br /> So the game got nothing wrong, it was George Lucas who did to add drama to Indiana Jones. Messerach didn't went through absolutely nothing that should particularly show as damage in the corpse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T15:44:33-07:00","id":1457653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394634-messerach?p=1457528#post1457528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, the people that used real mummies to make remedies (yes. That was a thing. That was a thing until the 20th century. On the black market that is STILL a thing) had to use regular meat and bone grinders to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, i've always asked myself how some Setites and part of their followers might feel about this particular niche but quite lucrative sector of the black market.<br /> <br /> But speaking of funny little details, always found the whole &quot;sarcophagus needs a special key to be opened, you can't just break it with Potence and a sledgehammer&quot; mighty suspicious - though i guess it's such an ingrained videogame gimmick most people just gloss it over without thinking much about it.<br /> <br /> Also, nobody ever used Auspex 3, the Spirit's Touch, on the damn thing? Seems like a natural thing for any kindred to consider while investigating the sarcophagus and its contents - among other things, to be sure whatever was inside did not escape already then closed the lid, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-26-2021, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}